category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":0,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 16.8%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 3.83"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":131.24,"default_fair_val":131.24,"premium_pct":-27.2,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":8.6,"pe_forward":7.6,"pb_trailing":2.5,"pb_forward":2.2,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":3.6,"fcf_to_ev":9.31,"fcf_to_mcap":6.91,"liab_to_assets":16.8,"cash_to_assets":53.4,"current_ratio":3.83,"roe":28.8,"roa":24,"moat":{"ticker":"ZM","period":"2027Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 在視訊通訊領域建立了強大的品牌認知度，使其在市場上具有一定的定價權。用戶習慣了 Zoom 的易用性和可靠性，即使面對競爭對手，也傾向於繼續使用。然而，視訊通訊作為一種服務，其本質上仍具備一定的商品化屬性，價格敏感度依然存在。Zoom 的品牌優勢使其能夠在不犧牲太多市場份額的情況下，維持相對穩定的價格，但要達到極高的定價權，仍需面對來自微軟 Teams 等整合性平台的挑戰。其品牌壁壘堅固，但非無懈可擊。","comment_en":"Zoom has established strong brand recognition in the video conferencing space, granting it a degree of pricing power. Users are accustomed to Zoom's ease of use and reliability, tending to stick with it despite competitors. However, video conferencing as a service inherently possesses some commoditized characteristics, and price sensitivity remains a factor. Zoom's brand strength allows it to maintain relatively stable pricing without sacrificing significant market share, but achieving exceptional pricing power still requires facing challenges from integrated platforms like Microsoft Teams. Its brand barrier is solid, but not impenetrable."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的核心競爭力在於其軟體技術和用戶體驗，而非依賴專利或特許經營權。雖然其技術創新可能受到專利的保護，但視訊通訊領域的技術迭代迅速，專利壁壘相對較弱。此外，該行業的監管障礙也較低，進入門檻不高。Zoom 的成功更多是依靠產品的卓越性能和市場先發優勢，而非受法律或監管保護的特許經營權。因此，在專利和監管壁壘方面，Zoom 的護城河較為薄弱。","comment_en":"Zoom's core competitiveness lies in its software technology and user experience, rather than relying on patents or regulatory exclusivity. While its technological innovations may be protected by patents, the rapid pace of technological evolution in the video conferencing sector makes patent barriers relatively weak. Furthermore, regulatory hurdles in this industry are also low, resulting in a low barrier to entry. Zoom's success is primarily driven by product excellence and first-mover advantage, not by protected franchises granted by law or regulation. Therefore, Zoom's moat in terms of patents and regulatory barriers is comparatively weak."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的轉換成本屬於中等水平。對於個人用戶和小型企業而言，轉換到其他視訊平台相對容易，因為學習新軟體的成本不高。然而，對於已經深度整合 Zoom 到其工作流程、擁有大量會議記錄和用戶習慣的企業客戶來說，轉換的成本會顯著增加。這包括重新培訓員工、調整 IT 基礎設施以及潛在的數據遷移問題。儘管如此，相較於 ERP 或 CRM 系統，Zoom 的轉換成本仍不算極高，但足以提供一定的客戶黏性。","comment_en":"Zoom's switching costs are moderate. For individual users and small businesses, switching to other video platforms is relatively easy, as the cost of learning new software is not high. However, for enterprise clients who have deeply integrated Zoom into their workflows and have extensive meeting history and established user habits, the cost of switching increases significantly. This includes retraining employees, adjusting IT infrastructure, and potential data migration issues. Nevertheless, compared to ERP or CRM systems, Zoom's switching costs are not extremely high, but they are sufficient to provide a degree of customer stickiness."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Zoom 展現了顯著的網絡效應。當越來越多的人使用 Zoom 開會時，其價值對每個參與者來說都會增加。一個公司或組織選擇 Zoom，往往是因為其合作夥伴、客戶或員工已經在使用該平台，這使得協作更加順暢。這種「人越多越好用」的特性，形成了正向循環，增加了新進入者的挑戰。尤其是在企業級市場，一旦 Zoom 成為內部溝通標準，其網絡效應將變得更加牢固，難以被取代。","comment_en":"Zoom exhibits significant network effects. As more people use Zoom for meetings, its value increases for every participant. When a company or organization chooses Zoom, it's often because their partners, clients, or employees are already using the platform, facilitating smoother collaboration. This 'the more users, the better it works' characteristic creates a virtuous cycle, increasing the challenge for new entrants. Particularly in the enterprise market, once Zoom becomes the internal communication standard, its network effects become more robust and difficult to displace."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 在規模經濟方面具有一定的優勢。隨著用戶基數的擴大，其固定成本（如伺服器維護、研發投入）可以分攤到更多的用戶身上，從而降低單位用戶的營運成本。此外，龐大的用戶群也使其在與雲端基礎設施供應商談判時擁有更強的議價能力。然而，視訊通訊服務的邊際成本相對較低，規模效應的邊際效益遞減。Zoom 的成本優勢主要體現在營運效率和採購談判上，而非生產製造的顯著差異。","comment_en":"Zoom possesses a certain advantage in economies of scale. As its user base expands, its fixed costs (such as server maintenance and R&D investment) can be spread across more users, thereby reducing the operational cost per user. Furthermore, a large user base also gives it stronger bargaining power when negotiating with cloud infrastructure providers. However, the marginal cost of video conferencing services is relatively low, and the marginal benefit of scale economies diminishes. Zoom's cost advantage is primarily reflected in operational efficiency and procurement negotiations, rather than significant differences in production manufacturing."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的業務模式高度依賴於軟體技術和全球互聯網基礎設施，並不存在獨特的地理位置或實物資產壁壘。其服務可以輕鬆地在全球範圍內提供，不受特定地理區域的限制。因此，Zoom 並沒有依賴任何特定的地理位置或獨特的實物資產來建立其競爭優勢。其價值在於技術和網絡，而非土地、礦產或特定地點的資源。","comment_en":"Zoom's business model relies heavily on software technology and global internet infrastructure, and it does not possess unique geographical locations or physical asset barriers. Its services can be easily provided globally, without being restricted by specific geographical areas. Therefore, Zoom does not depend on any particular geographic location or unique physical assets to build its competitive advantage. Its value lies in technology and network, not in land, minerals, or resources tied to specific locations."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Zoom 在營運效率方面表現出色，這在其財務數據中得到了體現（高 ROE、ROA、強勁的 FCF）。公司能夠有效地管理其基礎設施和營運成本，將資源集中在產品開發和用戶體驗的提升上。其軟體架構的設計也支持了大規模、高併發的會議需求，並能快速響應市場變化。這種高效的營運能力是其能夠在競爭激烈的市場中保持盈利能力和增長的重要因素。","comment_en":"Zoom excels in operational efficiency, as reflected in its financial data (high ROE, ROA, strong FCF). The company effectively manages its infrastructure and operating costs, focusing resources on product development and enhancing user experience. Its software architecture is designed to support large-scale, high-concurrency meeting demands and respond rapidly to market changes. This efficient operational capability is a crucial factor enabling it to maintain profitability and growth in a highly competitive market."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 展現了良好的資本配置能力。公司擁有充裕的現金儲備和極低的負債，這為其提供了財務上的靈活性，能夠應對市場波動或進行戰略投資。其強勁的自由現金流（FCF）表明公司能夠產生足夠的現金來支持營運、研發和潛在的併購。雖然 Zoom 可能不像傳統價值股那樣頻繁進行大規模股票回購，但其審慎的財務管理和對核心業務的持續投入，顯示了其資本配置的有效性。","comment_en":"Zoom demonstrates good capital allocation capabilities. The company possesses ample cash reserves and very low debt, providing it with financial flexibility to navigate market fluctuations or pursue strategic investments. Its strong free cash flow (FCF) indicates its ability to generate sufficient cash to support operations, R&D, and potential acquisitions. While Zoom may not engage in frequent large-scale share buybacks like traditional value stocks, its prudent financial management and sustained investment in its core business show effective capital allocation."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的客戶留存率相對較高，這得益於其產品的易用性、可靠性以及逐步建立的網絡效應。一旦用戶和企業習慣了 Zoom 的操作界面和功能，並將其整合到日常工作中，轉換到其他平台的意願就會降低。雖然市場上存在替代品，但 Zoom 持續的產品更新和對用戶體驗的關注，有助於維持客戶忠誠度。然而，若競爭對手提供更具吸引力的整合方案或顯著的價格優勢，客戶流失的風險依然存在。","comment_en":"Zoom's customer retention rate is relatively high, thanks to its product's ease of use, reliability, and the gradually building network effects. Once users and businesses become accustomed to Zoom's interface and features and integrate it into their daily operations, their willingness to switch to other platforms decreases. Although alternatives exist in the market, Zoom's continuous product updates and focus on user experience help maintain customer loyalty. However, if competitors offer more attractive integrated solutions or significant price advantages, the risk of customer churn remains."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的護城河耐久性面臨挑戰。雖然其品牌和網絡效應提供了一定的保護，但視訊通訊領域的技術變革迅速，且市場競爭激烈。微軟 Teams 等整合了通訊、協作和視訊功能的平台，對 Zoom 構成了持續的威脅。Zoom 需要不斷創新以維持其領先地位，並應對潛在的顛覆性技術或商業模式。其目前的優勢能夠維持一段時間，但長期來看，其耐久性取決於持續的創新能力和市場適應性。","comment_en":"Zoom's moat durability faces challenges. While its brand and network effects offer some protection, the video conferencing sector is characterized by rapid technological change and intense market competition. Platforms like Microsoft Teams, which integrate communication, collaboration, and video functionalities, pose a continuous threat to Zoom. Zoom needs to innovate constantly to maintain its leading position and counter potential disruptive technologies or business models. Its current advantages can last for a period, but in the long run, its durability depends on its sustained innovation capabilities and market adaptability."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Zoom 在視訊通訊領域建立了強大的品牌和顯著的網絡效應，使其在市場上佔據有利地位，並具備一定的客戶黏性與營運效率。其技術創新和良好的資本配置能力是重要的優勢。然而，Zoom 的護城河並非無懈可擊，其專利與監管壁壘較弱，轉換成本中等，且面臨來自整合性平台的激烈競爭，這影響了其長期耐久性。Zoom 的商業模式更接近於一種強大的「收費橋」，連接了全球用戶的溝通需求，但其獨特性和抗顛覆性仍有待時間考驗。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Zoom has established a strong brand and significant network effects in the video conferencing space, positioning it favorably in the market with considerable customer stickiness and operational efficiency. Its technological innovation and sound capital allocation are important strengths. However, Zoom's moat is not impenetrable; its patent and regulatory barriers are weak, switching costs are moderate, and it faces intense competition from integrated platforms, impacting its long-term durability. Zoom's business model more closely resembles a powerful 'toll bridge,' connecting global communication needs, but its uniqueness and resistance to disruption remain to be tested over time.","evidenceHash":"782d3f9b9bc8d55f50a49d8ca85f65e02f9726b415414bda78ac887237f67c20","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-01-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T10:20:23.108Z","evidenceHash":"54cff5f2ea3d5cb3fe195540f6988fb53eb10144e536ecc028dbbdcfb8ca15d4"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-01-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T10:20:23.108Z","evidenceHash":"54cff5f2ea3d5cb3fe195540f6988fb53eb10144e536ecc028dbbdcfb8ca15d4"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ZM.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ZM.png","website":"https://www.zoom.com","ceo":"Eric S. Yuan","full_time_employees":"7438","description":"Zoom Communications, Inc. provides a robust platform for enhancing communication and fostering collaboration. The company's global reach is organized into three primary operational regions: the Americas, the Asia Pacific, and Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA). Eric S. Yuan founded the enterprise in 2011, and its corporate headquarters are situated in San Jose, California.","description_en":"Zoom Communications, Inc. provides a robust platform for enhancing communication and fostering collaboration. The company's global reach is organized into three primary 